            <ArticleTitle>Carpal bone involvement in gout.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>971-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The deposition of gout tophi in the hand occurs relatively late in the disease. Involvement of carpal bone is rarely reported in the literature. We present a 40-year-old man with a long duration of gouty arthritis involving the carpal bones.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
